WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.730
- [Ryan] Hi, my name is Ryan Jones.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.250
I'm a senior project manager at TPGi,

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.330
and I'm also a JAWS user.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.050
Today I'm going to show
you a brief example

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.110
of using JAWS on a webpage.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.970
We'll show a good example of a webpage

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.530
that has accessibility built into it.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.160
And then an example of what happens

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.040
when you're on a webpage

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.260
that does not have accessibility.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.310
These samples are made by the W3C

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.950
who also makes the web standards.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.870
So I have Google Chrome
open and JAWS running,

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.540
and I'm just going to start down arrowing

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.690
through part of this particular webpage.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:34.677
And we'll hear what JAWS says.

00:00:34.677 --> 00:00:37.720
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Heading
level two navigation menu,

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.290
list of four items.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.670
- [Ryan] So JAWS told me I
just moved past a heading.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.350
And then it says I'm moving into a list

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.808
with four items in it.

00:00:44.808 --> 00:00:45.890
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Link Home.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.110
- [Ryan] Link home, which
means this is a link

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.010
that I could activate,

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.055
and the name of the link is "home".

00:00:51.055 --> 00:00:52.390
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Link News.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:53.647
- [Ryan] A link called "news".

00:00:53.647 --> 00:00:55.340
- [JAWS Screen Reader]
Visited link tickets.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.650
- [Ryan] A link called "tickets"
that I have visited before.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.265
So it says "visited link".

00:00:59.265 --> 00:01:00.230
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Survey.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.140
- [Ryan] The word "survey",

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.129
which is not a link, it's just text.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.270
- [JAWS Screen Reader] List end.

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:06.080
- [Ryan] And then I'm
at the end of the list.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.957
If I keep down arrowing.

00:01:06.957 --> 00:01:09.730
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Heading
level one Citylights Survey.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:10.690
- [Ryan] I get to a new heading

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:12.491
called "Citylights Survey".

00:01:12.491 --> 00:01:13.324
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Heading level two,

00:01:13.324 --> 00:01:16.760
This Week's Survey: More city
parks - a pain or a gain?

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.130
- [Ryan] So if I continue to arrow down,

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:19.420
I'll move through the survey,

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:22.120
but I'm going to jump forward
and find the edit boxes

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:23.530
where I know there are some information

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.240
that I will need to type in.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.137
So I'm going to press a JAWS
shortcut key to let me do that.

00:01:29.137 --> 00:01:29.970
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Name.

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.370
Edit has popup menu.

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:32.610
- [Ryan] And JAWS said "name",

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.170
and it says that it's an edit box

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.680
so that I know that I could
type something in here,

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.730
if I needed to.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.256
If I continue to move forward
through these fields...

00:01:40.256 --> 00:01:41.470
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Email address.

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:42.930
Edit has popup menu.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.337
- [Ryan] There's one for email address.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.600
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Retype email.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.000
Edit has popup menu.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.551
- [Ryan] I need to retype the email.

00:01:48.551 --> 00:01:49.470
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Submit button.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.290
- [Ryan] The submit button.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.960
There's another way that
I could bring up a list

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.850
of all of the form fields on this page,

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.803
assuming that they are labeled properly.

00:01:56.803 --> 00:01:58.850
- [JAWS Screen Reader]
Select a Form Field dialog.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.360
List one, list view.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.600
Submit button 15 of 15.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.930
- [Ryan] And I'm at
the bottom of the page.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.070
So if I scroll up the list,

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.370
I'll find all the form fields there.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:08.530
The names will make sense

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:12.075
because this page does have
accessibility built into it.

00:02:12.075 --> 00:02:12.908
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Escape.

00:02:12.908 --> 00:02:15.730
- [Ryan] Now I'm going to switch
over to this similar page,

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:16.563
same page,

00:02:16.563 --> 00:02:18.997
but it's going to not have
accessibility built into it.

00:02:18.997 --> 00:02:20.910
- [JAWS Screen Reader]
Welcome to Citylights.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:22.160
Inaccessible survey.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.460
- [Ryan] So this is the
inaccessible version.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.500
If I'm back on that same
navigation menu on this page

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.570
where there's things that
are not done properly,

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.134
let's hear what JAWS says.

00:02:31.134 --> 00:02:32.840
- [JAWS Screen Reader]
Unlabeled graphic graphic IMG

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:34.800
slash nav Home on mouse over.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.090
- [Ryan] So this was the
thing on the other page

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:37.923
that said home link.

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:41.059
Now it's giving me a bunch of gibberish.

00:02:41.059 --> 00:02:42.310
- [JAWS Screen Reader]
Unlabeled graphic graphic

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.800
IMG slash nav News on mouse over.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.020
- [Ryan] So these are images here

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.190
in this navigation menu

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:48.730
that are not properly labeled,

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.097
so JAWS doesn't know what to call them.

00:02:50.097 --> 00:02:51.462
- [JAWS Screen Reader]
Unlabeled graphic graphic

00:02:51.462 --> 00:02:54.080
IMG slash nav Facts on mouse over.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.523
- [Ryan] And I'm just
pressing the down arrow key.

00:02:56.523 --> 00:02:57.680
- [JAWS Screen Reader]
Unlabeled graphic graphic

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.300
IMG slash nav Survey on mouse over.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.730
Citylights Survey.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.440
This Week's Survey: More city-

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.370
- [Ryan] JAWS did not tell me
that there were headings here

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:09.160
because this text was not
marked up with the heading text.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.230
In a similar example,

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.380
if I bring up the same list of form fields

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.927
that I used on the previous page...

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:16.150
- [JAWS Screen Reader]
Select a form field dialog.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.860
List one, list view.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.060
Unlabeled one combo box, quick menu,

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.060
one of 14.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.730
- [Ryan] Instead of the nice
properly labeled form fields

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:24.907
that I had on the other page...

00:03:24.907 --> 00:03:26.750
- [JAWS Screen Reader]
Radio button not checked.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.190
Radio button not checked.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:29.630
Radio button not checked.

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:30.950
- [Ryan] I'm not getting any labels

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.950
on these particular form fields,

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.480
because they were not properly labeled

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.387
for accessibility.

00:03:35.387 --> 00:03:36.620
- [JAWS Screen Reader] Escape.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:37.640
- [Ryan] As the screen reader user,

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.670
I can use all kinds of
different shortcut keys

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:41.400
to move around this page,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.840
move to different form fields,

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.538
links, buttons, headings.

00:03:44.538 --> 00:03:46.700
All of those things that
I can move to, though,

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.434
have to have been coded
properly for accessibility,

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:52.370
in order for the shortcut keys to work,

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.670
and in order for JAWS
to read the information.

